2026-11-23T11:14:32 | Claude chunk H | found | Root cause of the "no event handler with ID 121" in SubtasksInTheLinkedView: a late Changed from the tick's write.\nThe tick (RunInBackground) tells the pages through Workspace.NotifyWritten after a 300 ms real-time quiet time. That Changed lands during the later edit/add steps, the page reloads and redraws, and the add line's @bind input gets a new onchange handler id.\nProved under CPU load (20 busy loops, 60 repetitions of the test per run): failed 1-2 in 60 per run, always the same id 121. A Changed trace showed the order: edit's Do-Changed, then the tick's BurstEnded-Changed at the moment of the failing step; Loads 1->3 with no render-count change seen by the test. Not a product bug (a redraw after a real change is correct), so the test must settle.
