2026-11-23T11:14:32 | Claude chunk H | done | Chunk H done, commit 0c46641 on agent/linked-subtasks-test (only TaskManager.Tests/UsingThePagesTests.cs).\nRoot cause: the tick in SubtasksInTheLinkedView is written in the background and the workspace tells the pages 300 ms later (NotifyWritten quiet time, real clock). That Changed lands during the edit/add steps; the page reloads and redraws and the add line's @bind input gets a new onchange handler id, so a Find that took id 121 before it fails (found at the "A fresh step" step). The redraw is correct behaviour, not a product bug.\nFix (test only): the test runs on a FakeTimeProvider (the workspace's quiet time and the page's 50 ms reload window both use it) and a local Settled() after the tick, the edit and the add: await workspace.DrainAsync (the write landed, the news is armed), time.Advance(1s) (the news is told, the window ends), await workspace.Resolved, await page.InvokeAsync(() => { }) (the draw has run). No sleeps, no retries.\nEvidence: under 20 busy loops, 60 repetitions per run, the old test failed in 4 of 5 runs (1-2 of 60); the fixed one 0 of 180. Final run: Passed 92, Failed 0 (the three classes).\nDeviation: none; scratch theory and instrumentation were removed before the commit.
